## The house

- **Store name** — {{ agents.store_name }}. The house signs itself **Maison Betty Jaletti** on products and packaging; both names refer to the same business. The vendor field on every product reads `Maison Betty Jaletti`.
- **House line** — *petits plaisirs, faits exprès*. Also used: *Little things, kept close.* and *Take the long way home.*
- **Where** — an American house, based in Virginia, United States. Sells in {{ agents.currency }}.
- **Why it exists** — the founder was named for two women called Betty: one who kept her paperbacks like secrets, spines cracked and margins argued in; one who held that anything worth doing was worth the good glass, fresh flowers, and no rush at all. The house exists to keep their opinion alive. The full letter is at `/pages/the-letter` ("Our Why").
- **How things are made** — in considered quantities, the unhurried way. An edition is finished when it is right, not when it is due. Parcels are packed by hand, by the house, before they go to the post.
- **Who it is for** — people who still do things the long way on purpose: who make the coffee themselves because they have the cup for it, highlight in ink without apology, and buy the bouquet for a Tuesday.

